WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.700
So Donald Trump's taxes are back in the news
and have actually been subpoenaed by the Manhattan

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.620
District Attorney State Prosecutors in Manhattan
have subpoenaed Donald Trump's accounting

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:16.910
firm demanding eight years of both Trump's
personal and business tax returns.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.699
Now, the first question we might ask is district
attorney, if a district attorney is issuing

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:28.980
a subpoena for Donald Trump's tax returns,
is this related to some kind of investigation?

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.920
And the answer is that yes, it turns out that
at the end of August, a criminal investigation

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.760
was opened up into those hush money payments
made by Donald Trump to mistresses.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.860
And I know many of us are completely fatigued
and sick of this hush money thing by now.

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.810
Um, and I'll sort of address that in a second.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.520
These are the payments that were made.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:53.239
The payments were made in a, in a literal
sense by Trump's now in prison, personal attorney

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:54.420
Michael Cohen.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.180
But of course they were made in service to
Donald Trump and Donald Trump as far as we

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.220
know, reimburse those payments to Michael
Cohen.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.899
So that's the answer to question one.

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:06.460
It's part of that invent a new criminal investigation.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:13.069
Question two is what's the full scope of this
Manhattan district attorney probe?

00:01:13.069 --> 00:01:19.149
Is it related only to the 2016 hush money
payments or is there some broader campaign

00:01:19.149 --> 00:01:22.599
finance or other investigation that this is
part of?

00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:24.240
We don't know the answer to that.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.009
We know that one legal question about the
hush money, uh, particularly the payment made

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:35.240
to stormy Daniels is did Donald Trump's business
call that illegal expense in their accounting,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.649
which would be number one, hilarious.

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:42.719
And number two potentially illegal and a felony
if it was done to conceal some other crime

00:01:42.719 --> 00:01:46.899
like tax evasion or bank fraud or in the service
of some additional crime.

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:48.579
So we'll figure that out.

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:49.579
Maybe someday.

00:01:49.579 --> 00:01:54.200
But let's get more to what matters here and
what doesn't matter.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.149
I understand we are mostly sick of this entire
hush money payment thing.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:04.859
The hush money payments themselves as a way
to punish Donald Trump or make him suffer

00:02:04.859 --> 00:02:07.289
consequences for the things that he did.

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:09.369
I believe that that ship has sailed.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:16.241
We can, as a practical matter, vote Donald
Trump out way faster than the hush money payment

00:02:16.241 --> 00:02:18.989
investigation could even potentially remove
him from office.

00:02:18.989 --> 00:02:19.989
It just not gonna happen.

00:02:19.989 --> 00:02:21.820
We shouldn't even be thinking about that.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:26.969
Then we get to the content of the tax returns
themselves.

00:02:26.969 --> 00:02:28.459
That's actually what we're interested in.

00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:36.099
Now, that being said, this is a district attorney
subpoena for an investigation if they get

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:41.200
the tax returns, meaning if the grand jury
gets those tax returns, they would not even

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.109
go public unless they're leaked.

00:02:43.109 --> 00:02:47.930
Of course, unless they end up becoming evidence
at a trial.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.829
That is also extremely unlikely to happen.

00:02:50.829 --> 00:02:55.829
So I don't really see this as something to
be optimistic about in terms of the material

00:02:55.829 --> 00:03:01.920
getting to us for our review, but it's yet
another thing that could trigger Donald Trump.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:02.950
First of all.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:08.739
Secondly, every time that we do hear anything
related to the content of Donald Trump's taxes,

00:03:08.739 --> 00:03:12.670
it's been something that makes him look terrible,
so there is still the potential here that

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:17.359
if any of this is released in any way leaked
or otherwise, it's going to contain extremely

00:03:17.359 --> 00:03:19.150
damaging information about Donald Trump.

00:03:19.150 --> 00:03:23.969
Remember that when the summaries of Donald
Trump's tax returns got out, we learned that

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:28.109
he lost just like insane amounts of money
and they put out his attorney or someone put

00:03:28.109 --> 00:03:29.790
out a statement saying, oh, this is all calculated.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:33.720
You know, he's gaming the system and this
is all because he's such a great businessman.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:39.280
People who were not working for Trump, who
know about tax law and accounting looked at

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.280
it and said, no, no, no.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.980
This is just the guys really losing a lot,
a lot of money, or he lost a lot of money

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:44.980
in that time.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.670
It would not be for the tax benefits.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:51.700
We also learned from other tax disclosures
of Trump that we got awhile ago that Donald

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:57.420
Trump's dad had financed a lot of Donald Trump's
failures, that we call that rich dad bails

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.420
me out.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.000
Just like the height of privilege for someone
claiming to be a self made man.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.969
So this could be interesting if something
like that comes out.

00:04:04.969 --> 00:04:09.629
It could be interesting in that even just
fighting, it could become a big story and

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:12.040
expensive Donald Trump, which would be just
delightful.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:18.070
But as far as getting rid of Trump, as far
as exposing criminality, the strategy remains

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:22.760
the same one that it's been for more than
a year, vote Trump out in November of 2020

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:28.449
he'll be gone when a new president is inaugurated
in January of 2021 and it will be far, far

00:04:28.449 --> 00:04:33.930
more efficient than any of these ideas related
to tax returns or the 25th amendment or impeachment.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:38.699
I know the fans of each of those individually
will say no, those are great ideas, David,

00:04:38.699 --> 00:04:42.450
and they may well be, but they're not going
to get Trump out any faster than just voting

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.450
him out in November.

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:43.490
If you disagree with me, let me know.

